.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MDC2 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_mdc2
.Nd MDC-2 For EVP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo EVP_mdc2
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
MDC-2 (Modification Detection Code 2 or Meyer-Schilling) is a
cryptographic hash function based on a block cipher.
This implementation is only available with the legacy provider.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_mdc2()
The MDC-2DES algorithm of using MDC-2 with the DES block cipher.
It produces a 128-bit output from a given input.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling this function multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-MDC2 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
ISO/IEC 10118-2:2000 Hash-Function 2, with DES as the underlying block
cipher.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr evp 7 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
.Xr EVP_DigestInit 3
